[{"category":"section","location":"api/","page":"API","text":"","title":"API"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#FEM.AbstractFEBasis","page":"API","text":"AbstractFEBasis\n\nAbstract supertype for finite element basis.\n\nConcrete subtypes: Lagrange{Deg, Dim}, Hermite{Deg, Dim}.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"FEM.AbstractFEBasis"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#FEM.Hermite","page":"API","text":"Hermite{Deg, Dim} <: AbstractFEBasis\n\nHermite basis of degree Deg in spatial dimension Dim.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"FEM.Hermite"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#FEM.Lagrange","page":"API","text":"Lagrange{Deg, Dim} <: AbstractFEBasis\n\nLagrange basis of degree Deg in spatial dimension Dim.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"FEM.Lagrange"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#FEM.basis_functions-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{Deg}, Tuple{Lagrange{Deg, 2}, T, T}} where {Deg, T<:Real}","page":"API","text":"basis_functions(::Lagrange{Deg, 2}, ξ, η)\n\nTensor-product Lagrange basis functions on the reference element [-1,1] × [-1,1].\n\nArguments\n\nξ::T: First coordinate in the reference element\nη::T: Second coordinate in the reference element\n\nReturns\n\nSVector{(Deg+1)²,T}: Values of all basis functions\n\nNode Layout (Deg = 1)\n\n3 --- 4\n|     |\n1 --- 2\n\nNode Layout (Deg = 2)\n\n7 --- 8 --- 9\n|     |     |\n4 --- 5 --- 6\n|     |     |\n1 --- 2 --- 3\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"FEM.basis_functions"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#FEM.basis_functions-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{Hermite{3, 1}, T}} where T<:Real","page":"API","text":"basis_functions(::Hermite{3, 1}, ξ)\n\nCubic Hermite basis functions on the reference element [-1, 1].\n\nArguments\n\nξ::T: Coordinate in the reference element [-1, 1]\n\nReturns\n\nSVector{4,T}: Values [H₁(ξ), H₁'(ξ), H₂(ξ), H₂'(ξ)]\n\nNode Layout\n\n1:2 ---- 3:4\n\nEach node has 2 DOFs: (u, du/dξ)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"FEM.basis_functions"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#FEM.basis_functions-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{Hermite{3, 2}, T, T}} where T<:Real","page":"API","text":"basis_functions(::Hermite{3, 2}, ξ, η)\n\nBicubic Hermite basis functions on the reference element [-1,1] × [-1,1].\n\nArguments\n\nξ::T: First coordinate in the reference element\nη::T: Second coordinate in the reference element\n\nReturns\n\nSVector{16,T}: Values of all 16 basis functions\n\nNode Layout\n\n 9:12 ---- 13:16\n  |          |\n  |          |\n 1:4  ----  5:8\n\nEach corner node has 4 DOFs: (u, ∂u/∂ξ, ∂u/∂η, ∂²u/∂ξ∂η)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"FEM.basis_functions"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#FEM.basis_functions-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{Lagrange{1, 1}, T}} where T<:Real","page":"API","text":"basis_functions(::Lagrange{Deg, 1}, ξ)\n\nLagrange basis functions on the reference element [-1, 1].\n\nDeg Nodes Layout Returned SVector\n1 1-----------2 (frac1-ξ2 frac1+ξ2)\n2 1-----2-----3 (fracξ(ξ-1)2 (1-ξ)(1+ξ) fracξ(ξ+1)2)\n3 1---2---3---4 (frac(3ξ+1)(3ξ-1)(1-ξ)16 frac(27ξ-9)(ξ+1)(ξ-1)16 frac(27ξ+9)(ξ+1)(1-ξ)16 frac(3ξ+1)(3ξ-1)(ξ+1)16)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"FEM.basis_functions"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#FEM.basis_functions_derivatives-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{Deg}, Tuple{Lagrange{Deg, 2}, T, T}} where {Deg, T<:Real}","page":"API","text":"basis_functions_derivatives(::Lagrange{Deg, 2}, ξ, η)\n\nDerivatives of tensor-product Lagrange basis functions.\n\nArguments\n\nξ::T: First coordinate in the reference element\nη::T: Second coordinate in the reference element\n\nReturns\n\nTuple (∂ϕ/∂ξ, ∂ϕ/∂η) where:\n∂ϕ/∂ξ::SVector{(Deg+1)²,T}: Derivatives ∂ϕᵢ/∂ξ\n∂ϕ/∂η::SVector{(Deg+1)²,T}: Derivatives ∂ϕᵢ/∂η\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"FEM.basis_functions_derivatives"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#FEM.basis_functions_derivatives-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{Hermite{3, 1}, T}} where T<:Real","page":"API","text":"basis_functions_derivatives(::Hermite{3, 1}, ξ)\n\nDerivatives of cubic Hermite basis functions with respect to ξ.\n\nArguments\n\nξ::T: Coordinate in the reference element [-1, 1]\n\nReturns\n\nSVector{4,T}: Derivatives [dH₁/dξ, dH₁'/dξ, dH₂/dξ, dH₂'/dξ]\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"FEM.basis_functions_derivatives"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#FEM.basis_functions_derivatives-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{Hermite{3, 2}, T, T}} where T<:Real","page":"API","text":"basis_functions_derivatives(::Hermite{3, 2}, ξ, η)\n\nDerivatives of Bicubic Hermite basis functions.\n\nArguments\n\nξ::T: First coordinate in the reference element\nη::T: Second coordinate in the reference element\n\nReturns\n\nTuple (∂ϕ/∂ξ, ∂ϕ/∂η) where:\n∂ϕ/∂ξ::SVector{16,T}: Derivatives ∂ϕᵢ/∂ξ\n∂ϕ/∂η::SVector{16,T}: Derivatives ∂ϕᵢ/∂η\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"FEM.basis_functions_derivatives"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#FEM.basis_functions_derivatives-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{Lagrange{1, 1}, T}} where T<:Real","page":"API","text":"basis_functions_derivatives(::Lagrange{Deg, 1}, ξ)\n\nLagrange basis functions derivatives on the reference element [-1, 1].\n\nDeg Nodes Layout Returned SVector\n1 1-----------2 (-frac12 frac12)\n2 1-----2-----3 (ξ-frac12 -2ξ ξ+frac12)\n3 1---2---3---4 (fracξ(18-27ξ)+116 frac-27-ξ(18-81ξ)16 frac27-ξ(18+81ξ)16 fracξ(18+27ξ)-116)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"FEM.basis_functions_derivatives"},{"category":"section","location":"","page":"Home","text":"This package provides basic functionalities for FEM codes.","title":"Home"}]
